Wait: capture-phase listener on root for bubbling events: our handler `#handleCapturedEvent` returns early if `event.bubbles`. But if event is `drop` with `bubbles: true`, capture listener runs at root, returns early; then event continues to target, bubbles back to root, Stimulus action listener (bubble) runs. Good.
For non-bubbling event dispatched on descendant: capture listener runs at root (capture phase) and handles; event doesn't bubble, so no duplicate. Good.
For non-bubbling event dispatched directly on root: capture listener runs at root (target phase) and handles; fine.
For events with `bubbles: false` but `composed: true` crossing shadow DOM? not relevant.

One issue: Stimulus actions are attached to root with bubble-phase; for non-bubbling event, no action. Capture handles. Good.

Another issue: `#handleCapturedEvent` for non-bubbling event uses `handlers[event.type]?.call(this, event)`. Method references `this.dragStart` are prototype methods; calling with `.call(this, event)` works. Good.

